STEP-3 GREEN — the MCP query seam is now enumerable from production. worker-adf39ce7.

`apps/daemon/src/mcp-dispatch-port.ts` 165 -> 212 lines (cap 250, no line over 100 chars). The four literal `envelope["queryKind"] === "..."` branches are gone; each body moved VERBATIM into a named `QueryHandler` — same refusal bytes, same `context?.credential ?? config.fallbackCredential ?? null` resolution repeated inline exactly as before (NOT extracted to a helper, so nothing about credential resolution changed shape), same `queryRefusal()` when `config.affordances`/`config.graph` is absent, same `bytesOf(authenticated)` / `eventStreamRefusal(...)` returns in events.read.

NEW SEAM:
  type QueryHandler = (envelope, context, config) => Uint8Array          (:68-72)
  const QUERY_HANDLERS: Readonly<Record<string, QueryHandler>> = Object.freeze({...})   (:146-151)
    keys exactly: events.read, graph.get, graph.preview, work.get_context
  const SERVED_QUERY_KINDS = Object.freeze([...Object.keys(QUERY_HANDLERS)].sort())     (:153-155)
  export function servedMcpQueryKinds(): readonly string[]                (:163-165)
DISPATCH is now three lines with no literal kind anywhere:
  const kind = envelope["queryKind"];
  const handler = typeof kind === "string" ? QUERY_HANDLERS[kind] : undefined;
  return handler === undefined ? queryRefusal() : handler(envelope, context, config);

TWO INDEPENDENT ENUMERATIONS PRESERVED ON PURPOSE. `mcp-tool-allowlist.ts` does NOT import `servedMcpQueryKinds`; `MCP_SERVED_QUERY_KINDS` stays the hand-kept ADVERTISED oracle and `WIRED_KINDS` is untouched. Its doc comment was rewritten to say why: importing the served set would collapse both sides into one enumeration and make the parity assertion tautological. The port's own doc comment now records that the query half routes through one frozen table and is compared in both directions.

